1
00:00:00,506 --> 00:00:07,450
Narrator: Forever 21 was a fast-fashion pioneer, known for selling trendy clothes at rock bottom-prices.&nbsp;

2
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:10,370
Really cheap. Really cute.Oh my gosh, I love this!

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:16,841
Narrator: At its peak, the company had more than 800 physical stores and over $4 billion in sales.&nbsp;

4
00:00:16,841 --> 00:00:22,711
But now, the fast-fashion kingpin is toppling from competition within its own industry.

5
00:00:22,711 --> 00:00:30,715
The company has filed for bankruptcy for the second time, forcing it to shutter stores across the U.S. and lay off hundreds of employees.

6
00:00:30,715 --> 00:00:34,651
So, what went wrong?

7
00:00:34,651 --> 00:00:46,336
The story of Forever 21 started when a couple from Korea pulled together $11,000 in savings to open the first store in Los Angeles in 1984, calling it Fashion 21.&nbsp;

8
00:00:46,336 --> 00:00:57,097
Teen apparel retail has been around for decades, and Aeropostale or Abercrombie or Gap, they're definitely the stalwarts of teen apparel.

9
00:00:57,097 --> 00:01:10,503
I think the difference with Forever 21 is that when retailers like them came along, they were on top of the latest trends and styles much faster than retailers had been in the past.

10
00:01:10,503 --> 00:01:13,142
Narrator: Fast fashion wasn't a novel trend.&nbsp;

11
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:21,529
Competitors like Zara and Topshop were already selling similar products, but Forever 21 offered cheaper prices to consumers.

12
00:01:21,529 --> 00:01:28,457
Sweatshirts, button downs, you name it, Forever 21 probably had it, and for cheap.

13
00:01:28,457 --> 00:01:31,586
They would carry very trendy styles.

14
00:01:31,586 --> 00:01:36,897
Styles that, you know, you would see in designer clothing stores that were priced much higher.

15
00:01:36,897 --> 00:01:42,937
So this allowed a very fashion-conscious consumer to buy these types of apparel.

16
00:01:42,937 --> 00:01:55,203
Around 12% of teen consumers listed Forever 21 as their favorite brand in 2011, and sales for the retailer peaked at more than $4 billion in 2014.&nbsp;

17
00:01:55,203 --> 00:01:59,137
Forever 21's success quickly took the brand global.&nbsp;

18
00:01:59,137 --> 00:02:11,092
The retailer opened more than 200 stores internationally, and at least 70 of those stores were 35,000 square feet or larger, including a 90,000-square-foot store in Times Square.

19
00:02:11,092 --> 00:02:13,588
But expansion came at a cost.

20
00:02:13,588 --> 00:02:24,800
The big spaces, 35,000 square feet, that was something that they really emphasized and they really believed in, but that also meant that they had to have a lot of inventory.

21
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:30,588
Over time, that became a financial drain for the company and wasn't so easy to manage.

22
00:02:30,588 --> 00:02:39,303
In 2019, Forever 21 filed for bankruptcy, citing its rapid international expansion and underperformance as key reasons.&nbsp;

23
00:02:39,303 --> 00:02:46,500
Stores in Canada, Europe, and Asia lost $10 million on average in 2018 and 2019.&nbsp;

24
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:55,517
It wasn't just international sales that plummeted for Forever 21, it was also sales in U.S. malls, where the fast-fashion retailer was a major tenant.

25
00:02:55,517 --> 00:03:00,065
That drop stems from the rise in e-commerce and the COVID-19 pandemic.

26
00:03:00,065 --> 00:03:03,616
They were very slow to adapt to e-commerce.

27
00:03:03,616 --> 00:03:09,859
By the time they filed for bankruptcy, only 16% of their sales were through e-commerce.

28
00:03:09,859 --> 00:03:18,289
And at that point, you know, a lot of companies had already made e-commerce a much stronger part of their offering.

29
00:03:18,289 --> 00:03:26,968
Forever 21 continued to hemorrhage cash, to the tune of $120 million, just one month after filing for bankruptcy. Forever 21

30
00:03:26,968 --> 00:03:36,562
That's when licensing firm Authentic Brands Group and real estate companies Simon Property Group and Brookfield Property Partners joined forces to buy Forever 21.

31
00:03:36,562 --> 00:03:42,677
These mall owners were concerned. If you lose your biggest stores, who's gonna come into your malls?

32
00:03:42,677 --> 00:03:45,724
And then what does that mean about your other tenants?

33
00:03:45,724 --> 00:03:56,427
Part of the proposition was that with Simon and Brookfield, they're gonna be more flexible about rents because they are the landlords and they might tie the rents to the revenue.

34
00:03:56,427 --> 00:04:01,481
You're giving the retailer a bit more wiggle room when things aren't going so well.

35
00:04:01,481 --> 00:04:13,347
Authentic Brands is known for scooping up many fallen legacy brands, like Aeropostale, Brooks Brothers, and Reebok, and attempting to save them from extinction by licensing the brands to the highest bidder.&nbsp;

36
00:04:13,347 --> 00:04:16,465
The company declined to comment on this story.

37
00:04:16,465 --> 00:04:31,694
But even under new ownership, Forever 21 was up against a different challenge: Asian e-commerce powerhouses like Shein and Temu, which utilize thousands of factories in China to pump out new products at even lower prices.

38
00:04:31,694 --> 00:04:38,553
A Forever 21 graphic T-shirt sells for around $11, compared to just $5 at Shein.

39
00:04:38,553 --> 00:04:42,750
So Forever 21 formed a partnership with Shein in 2023.

40
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:57,124
Other retailers are going to have to learn what Shein's doing if they wanna compete because they're just faster and better understanding the customer.

41
00:04:57,124 --> 00:05:09,827
Shein offered Forever 21's lineup on its website, and for sure that got them some sales, but it didn't offset enough the loss from the competition from Shein.&nbsp;

42
00:05:09,827 --> 00:05:16,672
Forever 21 ultimately was undermined by companies like Shein that can do it faster and cheaper.

43
00:05:16,672 --> 00:05:24,444
Narrator: The remaining Forever 21 stores across the U.S. have begun liquidation sales, offering hefty discounts on remaining products.&nbsp;

44
00:05:24,444 --> 00:05:28,004
But that doesn't mean Forever 21 will be completely gone.

45
00:05:28,004 --> 00:05:36,678
Authentic Brands, they plan to continue to own Forever 21, and they have stores overseas that are not impacted by this bankruptcy.&nbsp;

46
00:05:36,678 --> 00:05:48,270
Possibly, someone like a Forever 21 served the purpose that both the mall owners and Authentic Brands wanted it to serve, which was that it continued to pull in traffic to the malls.

47
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:52,863
So that meant you had shoppers for all the other stores in Simon Property's malls.

48
00:05:52,863 --> 00:05:55,363
It's possible that, you know, they don't necessarily expect these companies to be profitable for them, you know, forever.

